WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.317
In this video, you will enter your home in a neighborhood contest.

00:00:04.317 --> 00:00:10.164
It is a short step by step form: photos, your address, and a name, and then you agree to the rules.

00:00:10.164 --> 00:00:11.860
It takes just a few minutes.

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:13.029
We start on the map.

00:00:13.929 --> 00:00:15.678
Start at SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:18.484 --> 00:00:21.001
On the home page, tap Use my location.

00:00:22.749 --> 00:00:23.731
Then tap Allow.

00:00:27.719 --> 00:00:30.957
Now look at the top of the map, beside the search box.

00:00:30.957 --> 00:00:33.782
See your picture, or your initial, in a circle?

00:00:33.782 --> 00:00:38.550
That is your account menu, and it is the doorway to everything else on the site.

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:38.962
Tap it.

00:00:40.564 --> 00:00:42.463
In the menu, tap Your contests.

00:00:44.125 --> 00:00:47.538
That is where the contests you run, and the homes you entered, live.

00:00:48.237 --> 00:00:50.493
This opens on your own page, Mine.

00:00:50.493 --> 00:00:53.975
To see every contest that is open today, tap Live now.

00:00:55.751 --> 00:00:59.101
Under Live now, find the contest, and tap Enter my home.

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:06.852
If you are not signed in yet, the form starts with a sign in step, with Google, or with your email.

00:01:06.852 --> 00:01:10.293
That keeps people from entering on someone else's behalf.

00:01:10.293 --> 00:01:12.547
This video picks up after you sign in.

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:15.624
The form takes you one screen at a time.

00:01:15.624 --> 00:01:16.493
First, photos.

00:01:16.493 --> 00:01:20.720
Show the lights at their best, so take them at night with everything on.

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:21.762
Tap Choose photos.

00:01:23.619 --> 00:01:28.419
You can pick up to eight, and the first one becomes the cover photo that people see first.

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:30.239
Tap Next.

00:01:32.188 --> 00:01:33.361
Next, your address.

00:01:33.361 --> 00:01:36.116
The city is already set to the contest's city.

00:01:36.116 --> 00:01:39.751
If your home is somewhere else, there is a link to change it.

00:01:39.751 --> 00:01:42.038
Type your street address and ZIP code.

00:01:42.038 --> 00:01:49.895
This is where the pin goes on the map, and visitors will see it so they can drive by, so only enter an address you are happy to share.

00:01:51.678 --> 00:01:52.983
Now the name to show.

00:01:52.983 --> 00:01:57.198
This is how your entry appears to voters, for example, The Kim family.

00:01:57.198 --> 00:02:01.768
You can add a line about your home, like, the roof is synchronized to music.

00:02:01.768 --> 00:02:04.499
It is optional, but it helps neighbors choose.

00:02:06.481 --> 00:02:08.977
The last screen lists what you entered.

00:02:08.977 --> 00:02:12.160
Each line has an Edit link, if you spot a mistake.

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:16.591
Tick the box to agree to the official rules, which you can read first.

00:02:16.591 --> 00:02:18.151
Then tap Submit my entry.

00:02:20.936 --> 00:02:21.898
You are entered!

00:02:21.898 --> 00:02:27.497
Organizers choose whether entries go on the map right away, or whether they review each one first.

00:02:27.497 --> 00:02:35.358
In this contest, the organizer reviews each entry, so it may take a little while to appear, and you will get an email when it is approved.

00:02:35.358 --> 00:02:40.278
You can enter more than one home, up to five in each contest, with Enter another home.

00:02:40.278 --> 00:02:43.784
And you can come back to edit your entry, which we cover next.

00:02:44.787 --> 00:02:47.070
Next up: Edit or withdraw your entry.
